assiz Glacier below Kintla Peak \u2014 the surveyors sketched a giant; almost nothing remains."}]}, {"id": "chief", "name": "Chief Mountain & the Front", "blurb": "The Lewis Overthrust ends in a wall over the plains \u2014 and one tower that walked away from it.", "keys": [{"lat": 48.85, "lon": -113.45, "d": 60, "az": 120, "el": 22, "cap": "The mountain front: a slab of Precambrian rock shoved fifty miles east over prairie shale."}, {"lat": 48.9328, "lon": -113.6097, "d": 14, "az": 95, "el": 14, "cap": "Chief Mountain \u2014 N\u00ednaiist\u00e1ko \u2014 a klippe left standing when erosion cut the thrust sheet behind it."}, {"lat": 48.9, "lon": -113.75, "d": 40, "az": 140, "el": 20, "cap": "Belly River country, running north to the Saskatchewan \u2014 the quiet corner of the sheet."}, {"lat": 48.96, "lon": -113.9047, "d": 30, "az": 170, "el": 16, "cap": "Waterton Lake crosses the 49th parallel; the boundary swath on this sheet became the world's first International Peace Park in 1932."}]}, {"id": "marias", "name": "Marias Pass & the Rails", "blurb": "The lowest crossing of the northern Rockies, found for the Great Northern in 1889 \u2014 the sheet's southern edge rides it.", "keys": [{"lat": 48.3183, "lon": -113.3556, "d": 24, "az": 110, "el": 16, "cap": "Marias Pass, 5,213 ft \u2014 John F. Stevens located it for the Great Northern in the December cold of 1889."}, {"lat": 48.285, "lon": -113.6, "d": 26, "az": 150, "el": 15, "cap": "Essex and the snowshed country, where the railway hugs the Middle Fork under avalanche slopes."}, {"lat": 48.4475, "lon": -113.2136, "d": 24, "az": 60, "el": 15, "cap": "Midvale \u2014 Glacier Park Station. The great timbered lodge opened here in 1913, and the tourists stepped off the Empire Builder's ancestors."}, {"lat": 48.4953, "lon": -113.9808, "d": 26, "az": 220, "el": 14, "cap": "Belton, the west gate \u2014 chalets from 1910, the year the park was born."}]}], "lines": [{"id": "lia", "chip": "Ice at its 1850 peak", "name": "Ice at 